==English==
{{was wotd|2007|September|1}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|præcocious||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:uder|la:praecox|tree=1}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*pekʷ-}}
From {{uder|en|la|praecox||premature, precocious, ripe before time, early ripe}}, from {{m|la| praecoquō||to ripen beforehand, ripen fully, also boil beforehand}}, from {{m|la|prae||before}} + {{m|la|coquō||to cook, boil, ripen}}. {{doublet|en|apricot}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|prĭ-kō'shəs}}, {{IPA|en|/pɹəˈkəʊʃəs/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-precocious.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|əʊʃəs|s=3}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Characterized by exceptionally early [[development]] or [[maturity]].
#: {{ant|en|serotinous}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''precocious''' plant was already blooming flowers by day 4.}}
#* {{RQ:Meredith Richard Feverel||15||Now those abominations whom you call '''precocious''' boys—your little pet monsters, doctor!—and who can wonder that the world is what it is? when it is full of them—as they will have no divine time to look back upon in their own lives, how can they believe in innocence and goodness, or be other than sons of selfishness and the Devil?}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=November 14, 2014
|author=Stephen Halliday
|title=Scotland 1-0 Republic of Ireland: Maloney the hero
|work=The Scotsman
|url=http://www.scotsman.com/sport/football/latest/scotland-1-0-republic-of-ireland-maloney-the-hero-1-3605869
|page=
|passage=Scotland’s most encouraging early source of an attacking threat was Andrew Robertson as the '''precocious''' left-back charged forward to good effect on a couple of occasions.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20150206195628/http://www.scotsman.com/sport/football/latest/scotland-1-0-republic-of-ireland-maloney-the-hero-1-3605869|archivedate=6 February 2015}}
#* {{RQ:Schuster Hepaticae|volume=V|page=5|text=Both groups, also, have already evolved '''precocious''' (intracapsular) spore germination.}}
# Exhibiting advanced [[skill]]s and [[aptitude]]s at an abnormally early age.
#: {{syn|en|prodigious|tranty}}
#: {{ant|en|altricial}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''precocious''' child began reading the newspaper at age four.}}

